<p>The idea is that every death will trigger a new set of logs, as every trip through is slightly different. Through this process, you are going to see the effect of living multiple lifetimes in Foundation custody,</p>
<p>At first, you see a man who is surprised to be seen for what he is, though the foundation is still not entirely sure what they've got. He initially chooses to keep returning to the Foundation out of curiosity, though he hints that he takes some &quot;breather lives&quot; in between.</p>
<p>As the novelty wears off and the foundation is better managing his containment, he starts to show signs of listlessness and boredom, slowly coming to terms with containment. He is a little confused to, as he doesn't remember living so many lives so similarly one after the other.</p>
<p>This culminates in a verbal fight with the lead researcher, after which he takes the first opportunity to suicide. The next set of logs show a changed man, one that has willingly followed the same path with major difference: the person he kills before becoming a D-Class is the same person that was the lead researcher.</p>
<p>Upon figuring this out, the foundation brings him in for an interview to ask about it. At this point I want to reference one of the written about XK class end of world scenarios, probably SCP 5000, where he lives a fairly successful life uncontained until the event. This wakes him up to the idea that he needs to live with containment, as the world literally ended when he left containment.</p>
<p>He says he wanted something new, so he came back but ensured a change in management for his wellbeing. At this point the mental mileage is really showing, and his demeanor is more exhausted than aggressive. He's willing to play ball, but wants to know if the foundation wants to be on his team.</p>
<p>It kinda ends on a cliff hanger, as he remains in containment but only just. The foundation still worries that something might happen to cause his death, and are doing what they can to find a way to indefinitely prolong his life to prevent the next loop from coming. The 05's are against using the fountain of life, and the ethics committee is of the opinion that a permanent death would be more ethical than eternal life, so they are looking into other methods to end or contain what they are classifying as a &quot;center of reality&quot; scenario.</p>

							</div>

								
					
